.TH BREWMASTER.PY 1 "2026-03-28" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brewmaster.py \- a smarter Homebrew upgrader with version diffs, retries, and logging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 brewmaster.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brewmaster.py
is an enhanced Homebrew upgrade wrapper that shows version diffs, checks outdated
formulae and casks in parallel, retries failed packages individually, skips pinned
packages, and logs every run to
.I ~/.brewmaster.log\c
\&.
.PP
Running without flags performs an interactive upgrade: it updates Homebrew metadata,
lists all outdated packages with version diffs, prompts for confirmation, then
upgrades each package individually, retrying failures before reporting a summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-approve all upgrades without an interactive prompt.
.TP
.BR \-\-greedy " (default)"
Include auto-updating casks when checking for outdated packages
.RB ( "brew outdated --cask --greedy" ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-greedy
Disable greedy cask checking. Only packages with a newer pinned version are shown.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-only
Report outdated packages with version diffs but do not perform any upgrades.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would be executed without running any of them.
Skips the confirmation prompt automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-skip " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Space-separated list of package names to exclude from the upgrade.
.RS
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --skip node python
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-formula\-only
Upgrade formulae only; skip all casks.
.TP
.B \-\-cask\-only
Upgrade casks only; skip all formulae.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a native macOS notification (via
.BR osascript )
when the run completes.
.TP
.B \-\-backup
Before upgrading, dump the current Homebrew state to a timestamped Brewfile at
.IR ~/.brewmaster_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.Brewfile .
Restore with:
.RS
.EX
brew bundle install --file=~/.brewmaster_backup_<timestamp>.Brewfile
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Number of retry attempts per package when an upgrade fails. Default is
.BR 2 .
.SH FEATURES
.SS Version Diff Display
Uses
.B brew outdated --json=v2
to show the installed and available version for each package:
.RS
.EX
  \(bu ffmpeg  6.1.0 \(-> 7.1.0
  \(bu node    20.11.0 \(-> 22.3.0
.EE
.RE
.SS Parallel Outdated Checks
Formula and cask outdated checks run concurrently in separate threads, reducing
wait time on slow connections.
.SS Per-Package Retries and Partial Failures
Each package is upgraded individually. On failure it is retried up to
.B --retries N
times. Remaining packages continue regardless, and all failures are collected
into a summary at the end.
.SS Pin Awareness
Reads
.B brew list --pinned
and automatically skips pinned formulae with a warning, e.g.:
.RS
.EX
  📌 Skipping pinned: python@3.11
.EE
.RE
.SS Upgrade Log
Every run appends timestamped entries to
.IR ~/.brewmaster.log :
.RS
.EX
[2026-03-28 14:05:01] --- BrewMaster run started ---
[2026-03-28 14:05:20] Upgraded formula: ffmpeg
[2026-03-28 14:05:45] FAILED cask: some-app -- error details
[2026-03-28 14:06:10] Run complete with 1 failure(s). Elapsed: 69.2s
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive upgrade (default):
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py
.EE
.TP
Auto-approve, skip node and python, notify on completion:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -y --skip node python --notify
.EE
.TP
Preview outdated packages with version diffs only:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --check-only
.EE
.TP
Dry run — print all commands, execute nothing:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --dry-run
.EE
.TP
Backup bundle, then upgrade formulae only:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --backup --formula-only
.EE
.TP
Upgrade casks only, retry each failure up to 3 times:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --cask-only --retries 3
.EE
.TP
Disable greedy cask detection, auto-approve:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --no-greedy -y
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster.log
Timestamped log of all BrewMaster runs, upgrades, and failures.
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.Brewfile
Bundle snapshots created by
.BR \-\-backup .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later, Homebrew (
.I https://brew.sh
), macOS.
.PP
The
.B \-\-notify
flag requires
.B osascript
(available by default on macOS).
.PP
The
.B \-\-backup
flag requires the
.B brew-bundle
tap (included with Homebrew by default).
.SH AUTHOR
Anirban Bagchi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1)
